**State of the story**

- The Lua gameplay API is in place in the new `engine_script` module (`engine/script/`), built on the vendored Lua 5.4.7. It covers `entity`, `transform`, `input`, `assets`, `physics` (raycast and sphere overlap), and `events`. Entities cross into Lua as handles, and a destroyed entity raises a controlled script error.
- The 15 headless test cases in `tests/src/script_lua_tests.cpp` (unit label) cover stack balance, type errors, and Lua exceptions.
- Passing gates, per the earlier log entry: Linux `ValidateVendor`, `linux-dev`, `linux-debug`, `linux-unit`, and `linux-asan` / `linux-sanitize` with no sanitizer report. Windows `ValidateVendor`, `win-dev`, `win-debug`, and `win-unit` all passed on the same source.
- Not run: `linux-gcc*`. The host has only GCC 9.4 and Clang 10, and Jolt needs GCC 11+ (or Clang 14+). Nothing newer than the last log entry has changed, and there is no container runtime to get a newer compiler. The CI Linux/GCC job has to close this gate.
- Not run: `engine_bench`. No benchmark harness exists yet (US-074), and this story has no GPU work.

